  "question": {
    "text": "In Kjeldahl's method for estimation of nitrogen, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CuSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> acts as :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "6DhC2",
      "text": "<p>Reducing agent</p>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HzcPE",
      "text": "Catalytic agent",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "61zGa",
      "text": "Hydrolysis agent",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ansJZ",
      "text": "Oxidising agent",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Kjeldahl's method is used for the estimation of nitrogen. The organic compound is heated with conc. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> in presence of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> and a little <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CuSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> to convert all the nitrogen into <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> raises the boiling point of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CuSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> catalyses the reaction.</p><p>Hence, B is the answer.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
